      "questionTextEn": "In an Oracle Database, when you execute `ORDER BY commission_pct` (without specifying `ASC`, `DESC`, `NULLS FIRST`, or `NULLS LAST`), where do rows with a `NULL` value in `commission_pct` appear in the output?",
