      "questionTextEn": "When `LISTAGG` concatenates so many rows that the resulting string exceeds the maximum `VARCHAR2` length (4000 bytes in standard mode) and no `ON OVERFLOW` clause is specified, what happens by default? And how can you safely truncate the string starting in Oracle 12cR2?",
