      "questionTextEn": "The `TICKETS` table has 10 million rows. The `STATUS` column is indexed by `IDX_TICKET_STATUS` and has extreme data skew: `'CLOSED'` accounts for `9,999,500` rows (99.995%), while `'OPEN'` accounts for only `500` rows (0.005%). To allow the CBO to recognize this skew so it chooses `INDEX RANGE SCAN` for `'OPEN'` and `TABLE ACCESS FULL` for `'CLOSED'`, what statistics object must the DBA gather on `STATUS`?",
