      "questionTextEn": "The `EMPLOYEES` table has a `NOT NULL` constraint on `EMPLOYEE_ID` and a composite index `IDX_EMP_DEPT_SAL` on `(DEPARTMENT_ID, SALARY)`. When executing the query below, why can Oracle return the result WITHOUT performing `TABLE ACCESS BY INDEX ROWID` (without touching the `EMPLOYEES` table)?",
