      "questionTextEn": "Two bank tellers simultaneously open the account screen for customer `ID = 500` (initial balance `10,000,000`). Teller 1 updates the balance to `12,000,000` and commits. Two seconds later, Teller 2 (still viewing the old `10,000,000` balance on screen) saves an update setting the balance to `9,000,000` and commits, completely overwriting Teller 1's `+2,000,000` deposit. What is this concurrency phenomenon called?",
